# build artifacts — NEVER commit generated model bytes / compiled weights
*.mlpackage/
*.mlmodelc/
*.aimodel/
*.aimodelc/
*.mpsgraphpackage/
_out/
_a*/
# loose model blobs (weights / adapters / checkpoints)
weight.bin
adapter*.bin
*.pt
*.hwx
# built harness + compile intermediates
swap
gen
*.o
__pycache__/
swap_multi
gen_qwen
.DS_Store

# ── Item 0 gate (2026-08-30): close the `git add -A` hazard ──────────────────
# Before this block 74,428 files (~30 GB) under vision/ and structured/ were one
# `git add -A` from being staged, including a 73.6 MB checkpoint whose `.keep`
# suffix defeated the `*.pt` rule above. These directories carry ZERO tracked
# files, so ignoring them wholesale cannot orphan anything.
vision/
structured/
graphify-out/
# suffix-evasion: any rule above defeated by a trailing tag
*.keep
*.bak
*.bak_*
# run logs and per-run scratch directories
*.log
qwen/_*/
# raster / media blobs — this repo tracks source (py, sh, mm, md, html)
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.webp
*.avif
# loose tensor dumps
*.f16
*.f32
*.npy
# build outputs
ce_qwen
logit_dump

# ── THE SUPPLEMENT IS A PUBLISHED ARTIFACT, NOT BUILD OUTPUT ─────────────────
# The blanket rules above (*.pt, *.log, *.png) are right for this repo's working
# dirs and WRONG for supplement_codebook/, whose whole job is to be pulled and
# run: the paper's checkpoint is a .pt, G6's corpus is 48 .png, the green gate
# runs are .log, fvmlib_check is a .txt. Without these negations 62 of its 96
# files vanish silently and a reader clones something that cannot run.
# ⛔ Scoped to this one directory on purpose. Do not widen.
!supplement_codebook/**/*.pt
!supplement_codebook/**/*.txt
!supplement_codebook/**/*.log
!supplement_codebook/**/*.png
# ...but its scratch/run outputs still stay out:
supplement_codebook/_gate_web.log
supplement_codebook/gate_run.log
supplement_codebook/gate_run_tierB.log
supplement_codebook/_demo_acceptance.json
supplement_codebook/data_codebook/
supplement_codebook/_adapters/
supplement_codebook/_mlc_shadow/
supplement_codebook/_demo/
